<title>FINLAND: FINNISH MARCH NEW PRIVATE CAR SALES UP 6 PCT YR/YR.</title>
<headline>FINNISH MARCH NEW PRIVATE CAR SALES UP 6 PCT YR/YR.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Registrations in Finland of new private cars increased 6.2 percent year-on-year in March to 8,866 units, the Information Centre of the Automobile Branch said in its monthly review on Monday.  </p>
<p>It gave the following figures:</p>
<p>				     change			  change</p>
<p>		  March '97     yr/yr pct  Jan-March '97  yr/yr pct</p>
<p> Private cars    8,866	  +6.2	   30,262	 +3.1</p>
<p> Vans		  859	 +20.3	    2,828	+24.9</p>
<p> Lorries	     360	 +44.0	    1,027	+16.7</p>
<p> Buses		  42	  +/-0		136	 -4.2</p>
<p> Total	    10,127	  +8.3	   34,253	 +5.0</p>
<p>--Helsinki newsroom +358-9-680 50 245, e-mail news@reuters.fi</p>
</text>
